{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","statement":"Django's translation work is coordinated at Transifex.","source_span":"The translation work is coordinated at `Transifex`_."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","statement":"Translations from Transifex are only integrated into the Django repository at the time of a new feature release.","source_span":"Translations from Transifex are only integrated into the Django repository at the time of a new :term:`feature release <Feature release>`."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","statement":"Django tries to update translations a second time during one of the following patch releases, depending on the translation manager's availability.","source_span":"We try to update them a second time during one of the following :term:`patch release <Patch release>`\\s, but that depends on the translation manager's availability."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","statement":"To change locale format files, a pull request must be created against the Django Git main branch and a ticket opened with Component set to Translations and the \"has patch\" flag set.","source_span":"Open a ticket in Django's ticket system, set its ``Component`` field to ``Translations``, set the \"has patch\" flag, and include the link to the pull request."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","statement":"A locale's date, time, and number formatting particularities are described in conf/locale/<locale>/formats.py.","source_span":"You can also review ``conf/locale/<locale>/formats.py``. This file describes the date, time and numbers formatting particularities of your locale."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","statement":"Format files are not managed through the use of Transifex.","source_span":"The format files aren't managed by the use of Transifex."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","statement":"Translated documentation appears at https://docs.djangoproject.com/<language_code>/ once at least the docs/intro/* files are fully translated in that language.","source_span":"The translations will appear at ``https://docs.djangoproject.com/<language_code>/`` when at least the ``docs/intro/*`` files are fully translated in your language."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","statement":"Only translations for the latest stable Django release are updated on the documentation website.","source_span":"Only translations for the latest stable Django release are updated."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","fact_refs":[0],"question":"Where is Django's translation work coordinated?","answer":"Django's translation work is coordinated at Transifex."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","fact_refs":[1,2],"question":"When are Transifex translations integrated into the Django repository?","answer":"They are integrated at the time of a new feature release. Django tries to update them again during a following patch release, but that depends on the translation manager's availability."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What must you do to change a Django locale's format files?","answer":"You must create a pull request against the Django Git main branch, and open a ticket with the Component field set to Translations, the \"has patch\" flag set, and a link to the pull request."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Which file describes date, time, and number formatting particularities for a Django locale?","answer":"conf/locale/<locale>/formats.py describes the date, time and numbers formatting particularities of the locale."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","fact_refs":[5],"question":"Are Django's locale format files managed through Transifex?","answer":"No, format files aren't managed by the use of Transifex."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_localizing","fact_refs":[6,7],"question":"When do translated Django docs appear at docs.djangoproject.com/<language_code>/?","answer":"They appear once at least the docs/intro/* files are fully translated in that language, and only translations for the latest stable Django release are kept updated."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","statement":"If a contribution is more than one or two lines of code, the contributor has the option to sign the Contributor License Agreement (CLA).","source_span":"If your contribution is more than one or two lines of code, you have the option to sign the `CLA`_."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","statement":"Django has an eight-month release cycle, which gives plenty of time for a patch to be reviewed.","source_span":"Remember that Django has an eight-month release cycle, so there's plenty of time for your patch to be reviewed."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","statement":"When reviewing patches, contributors should try them out on a database other than SQLite where possible and relevant.","source_span":"Where possible and relevant, try them out on a database other than SQLite."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","statement":"If uncertain whether a ticket should be marked \"Ready For Check-in,\" a contributor can ask on the #contributing-getting-started channel on the Django Discord server.","source_span":"you might also try asking on the ``#contributing-getting-started`` channel in the `Django Discord server`_ to see if someone else can confirm your suspicions."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","statement":"The \"Needs tests\", \"Needs documentation\", and \"Patch needs improvement\" Trac flags should be unchecked once all review comments on a patch have been addressed.","source_span":"Review the ticket on Trac to ensure that the *Needs tests*, *Needs documentation*, and *Patch needs improvement* flags are unchecked once you've addressed all review comments."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","statement":"New contributors are advised to focus on one or two tickets at a time and see them through, rather than taking on many tickets at once.","source_span":"Focus on one or two tickets, see them through from start to finish, and repeat. The shotgun approach of taking on lots of tickets and letting some fall by the wayside ends up doing more harm than good."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","fact_refs":[0],"question":"When does a Django contributor have the option to sign the CLA?","answer":"If their contribution is more than one or two lines of code, they have the option to sign the Contributor License Agreement (CLA)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","fact_refs":[1],"question":"How long is Django's release cycle, and why is this mentioned to new contributors?","answer":"Django has an eight-month release cycle, which gives plenty of time for a patch to be reviewed, so contributors are told to be patient."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What database advice does Django give to people reviewing patches, besides testing on SQLite?","answer":"Where possible and relevant, reviewers should try patches out on a database other than SQLite."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","fact_refs":[3],"question":"Where can a new Django contributor ask if they're unsure about marking a ticket \"Ready For Check-in\"?","answer":"They can ask on the #contributing-getting-started channel on the Django Discord server."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Which three Trac flags should be unchecked once all review comments on a Django patch are addressed?","answer":"The \"Needs tests\", \"Needs documentation\", and \"Patch needs improvement\" flags should be unchecked."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_new-contributors","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What approach does Django's new-contributor guide recommend for how many tickets to work on at once?","answer":"Focus on one or two tickets at a time and see them through from start to finish, rather than taking on many tickets simultaneously."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","statement":"Setting up a Django development virtual environment requires a Python version of 3.12 or higher.","source_span":"$ # This needs to be >= 3.12\n$ python -V"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","statement":"Contributors clone their fork with git clone https://github.com/YourGitHubName/django.git and add the upstream remote https://github.com/django/django.git.","source_span":"$ git clone https://github.com/YourGitHubName/django.git\n$ cd django\n$ git remote add upstream https://github.com/django/django.git"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","statement":"Pre-commit hooks are installed by running python -m pip install pre-commit followed by pre-commit install, so formatting and linting run automatically before each commit.","source_span":"$ python -m pip install pre-commit\n$ pre-commit install"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","statement":"The Django test suite is only guaranteed to pass on the latest point release of each supported Python version.","source_span":"the test suite is only guaranteed to pass on the latest point release of each supported Python version."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","statement":"The \"vulture method\" is the process of looking for accepted Django tickets that haven't been touched in six months or longer.","source_span":"The vulture method is the process of looking for accepted tickets that haven't been touched in six months or longer."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","statement":"Vulture-able tickets are filtered by Triage stage = Accepted, Patch needs improvement = Yes, Created between 5 years ago and today, and Modified between 5 years ago and 6 months ago.","source_span":"* Triage stage = Accepted\n* Patch needs improvement = Yes\n* Created = between ``5 years ago`` and ``today``\n* Modified = between ``5 years ago`` and ``6 months ago``"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","statement":"To claim a Django ticket, click the \"Modify Ticket\" button, select the \"assign to\" radio button in the \"Action\" section, and click \"Submit changes.\"","source_span":"make yourself the owner by clicking the \"Modify Ticket\" button near the bottom of the page, selecting the \"assign to\" radio button in the \"Action\" section, and clicking \"Submit changes\"."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","statement":"To start a fresh branch for a ticket, run git fetch upstream then git checkout -b ticket_TicketNumber upstream/main.","source_span":"$ git fetch upstream\n$ git checkout -b ticket_TicketNumber upstream/main"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What minimum Python version is needed to set up a Django development virtual environment?","answer":"Python version 3.12 or higher is required."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What two git remotes does a contributor set up when starting to work on Django from their fork?","answer":"They clone their fork (e.g. https://github.com/YourGitHubName/django.git) as origin, then add https://github.com/django/django.git as the upstream remote."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","fact_refs":[2],"question":"How do you install pre-commit hooks for a Django contribution, and what do they do?","answer":"Run `python -m pip install pre-commit` then `pre-commit install`; this makes formatting and linting run automatically before each commit."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","fact_refs":[3],"question":"On which Python versions is the Django test suite guaranteed to pass?","answer":"Only on the latest point release of each supported Python version."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What is the \"vulture method\" for finding a Django ticket to work on?","answer":"It's the process of looking for accepted tickets that haven't been touched in six months or longer."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What Trac filters are used to find \"vulture-able\" Django tickets?","answer":"Triage stage = Accepted, Patch needs improvement = Yes, Created between 5 years ago and today, and Modified between 5 years ago and 6 months ago."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","fact_refs":[6],"question":"How do you claim ownership of a Django Trac ticket?","answer":"Click the \"Modify Ticket\" button, select the \"assign to\" radio button in the \"Action\" section, and click \"Submit changes.\""}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_sprint-quickstart","fact_refs":[7],"question":"What git commands create a new branch for working on a specific Django ticket number?","answer":"Run `git fetch upstream` followed by `git checkout -b ticket_TicketNumber upstream/main`, replacing TicketNumber with the actual Trac ticket number."}
